SOFTWARE ENGINEERING LAB EXTERNAL
COMPLETE COMMAND CHEAT SHEET
Git | Maven | Docker | Docker Compose | Kubernetes | Nagios | Ngrok | AWS EC2 | Ubuntu

Purpose:
A start-to-finish practical reference for common SE Lab External tasks. Commands are grouped by tool and ordered from setup to verification. Replace every value written as <PLACEHOLDER> with your own value. Do not type the angle brackets.

IMPORTANT TERMINAL NOTE
-----------------------
1. Git, Maven, Docker and Minikube commands can be run in Windows PowerShell/Command Prompt when the tools are installed, or in Ubuntu/Linux terminal.
2. Commands beginning with sudo are for Ubuntu/Linux terminals, including an Ubuntu EC2 SSH session.
3. YAML and Dockerfile examples must be saved in files with the exact filenames shown.
4. Keep Docker Desktop / Docker Engine running before Docker or Minikube tasks.
5. For a Maven application, inspect pom.xml to know whether it creates a JAR or WAR and which Java version it needs.
6. Never expose passwords, private keys, GitHub tokens or Docker Hub access tokens in public source code.

